  "response": "Purification and properties of two succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenases from Klebsiella pneumoniae (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2647149/)\nciteturn32search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 37.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; doi: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8.\n\n. 1989 Mar 24;990(3):225-31.\n\ndoi: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8.\n\n# Purification and properties of two succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenases from Klebsiella pneumoniae\n\nM Sanchez^{  1 }, J Fernández, M Martin, A Gibello, A Garrido-Pertierra\n\n\n  * ^{1} Departamento de Bioquímica, Facultad de Veterinaria, Universidad Complutense, Madrid, Spain.\n\n  * PMID: 2647149\n  * DOI: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# Purification and properties of two succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenases from Klebsiella pneumoniae\n\nM Sanchez et al. Biochim Biophys Acta. 1989.\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat [Select]\n\n[Button: Biochim Biophys Acta ]\n\nActions\n\n  * Search in PubMed\n  * Search in NLM Catalog\n  * Add to Search\n\n. 1989 Mar 24;990(3):225-31.\n\ndoi: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8.\n\n### Authors\n\nM Sanchez^{  1 }, J Fernández, M Martin, A Gibello, A Garrido-Pertierra\n\n### Affiliation\n\n  * ^{1} Departamento de Bioquímica, Facultad de Veterinaria, Universidad Complutense, Madrid, Spain.\n\n  * PMID: 2647149\n  * DOI: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n[Button: Full text links ]Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat [Select]\n\n## Abstract\n\nTwo forms of succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase have been isolated in Klebsiella pneumoniae M5a1. The two enzymes could be separated by filtration on Sephacryl S-300 and their apparent molecular weights were approx. 275,000 and 300,000. The large enzyme is specific for NADP. The smaller enzyme, which is induced by growth on 3-hydroxyphenylacetic acid, 4-hydroxyphenylacetic acid, 3,4-dihydroxyphenylacetic acid and gamma-aminobutyrate, has been purified to 96% homogeneity by affinity chromatography. The NAD-linked succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase was able to use NADP as cofactor. Its induction is coordinated with 3- and 4-hydroxylase, the enzymes which initiate degradation of 3- and 4-hydroxyphenylacetic acid. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPurification and properties of two succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenases from Klebsiella pneumoniae (https://openalex.org/W2057162091)\nciteturn32search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 37.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; DOI: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8\n# Purification and properties of two succinic semialdehyde dehydrogenases from Klebsiella pneumoniae\n\nOpenAlex ID: W2057162091\n\nDOI: 10.1016/s0304-4165(89)80038-8\n\nPMID: 2647149\n\nType: article\n\nYear: 1989\n\nPublication date: 1989-03-01\n\nLanguage: en\n\n## Source\n\nName: Biochimica et Biophysica Acta (BBA) - General Subjects\n\nISSN-L: 0304-4165\n\nISSN: 0304-4165, 1872-8006\n\nPublisher: Elsevier BV\n\n## Citation\n\nVolume: 990\n\nIssue: 3\n\nPages: 225–231\n\n## Article links\n\n  * Article website\n  * Location website\n\n## Authors\n\n  * Miguel Sánchez — Universidad Complutense de Madrid (ROR)\n  * Javier Fernández (ORCID) — Universidad Complutense de Madrid (ROR)\n  * Marı́a T. Martı́n-Romero (ORCID) — Universidad Complutense de Madrid (ROR)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe X-Ray Crystal Structure of Escherichia coli Succinic Semialdehyde Dehydrogenase; Structural Insights into NADP+/Enzyme Interactions (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2823781/)\nciteturn32search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 16.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Archives of biochemistry and biophysics Volume: 266 First page: 386 Last page: 396 Identifier: [pub-id-type: pmid] 3190233 Identifier: [pub-id-type: doi] [assigning-authority: pmc] 10.1016/0003-9861(88)90270-6 ... Biochim Biophys Acta Volume: 24 First page: 225 Last page: 2